{"game": "deep-rock-galactic", "language": "english", "appid": 548430, "month": "2019-07", "window": 1, "start_date": 1561939200, "end_date": 1562630399, "month_true_total": 1606, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-08-29 21:19:53 Pacific Daylight Time", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "53975703", "author": {"steamid": "76561198253495448", "personaname": "I'm too old for this", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198253495448/", "num_games_owned": 185, "num_reviews": 14, "playtime_forever": 11817, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 198, "last_played": 1766336372, "avatar": "8218a93ff3966b03af6cd350a283e05971a612ef"}, "language": "english", "review": "Picked this gem up on sale since I love dwarfs and have seen this game around for awhile. I was apprehensive to purchase an early access game after being burned in past. \n\nFew hours in, and I love it. Don’t be fooled by its simplistic gameplay; there is plenty to do to challenge yourself and “dig” deeper into the game. Lots of opportunity for great team work, memorable moments and lots of action! \n\nAnd the environments are beautiful. Simplistic in design for sure, but beautiful. And the mining aspect is a great addition. \n\nClasses all have a niche to fill, and there’s really no “meta” in the game from what I can tell and what I’ve been told by vets. It’s just a great game to get lost in, kill some bugs and mine some rare materials!\n\n10/10. Fun as any co-op game I’ve played.", "timestamp_created": 1562628046, "timestamp_updated": 1562628046, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1519804887", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "53975354", "author": {"steamid": "76561198287917785", "personaname": "Samo", "persona_stat